# Python ↔ Node SDK client parity (meaning / define)

When **Node** SDK client surfaces change — especially
`meaning` / `define` / `thesaurus` / `shapes` / `proposals` / `bundles` —
**Python must be updated in the same change set or an immediate follow-up PR**.
Do not ship Node-only for these APIs and leave `python/` behind.

## Paths

| Language | Client root |
| --- | --- |
| Node | `nodejs/src/client/` |
| Python | `python/src/loxtep/` |

Also update `nodejs/docs/sdk-mcp-mapping.md` (Node) and `python/README.md` +
`python/CHANGELOG.md` (Python) when methods are added.

## Required surfaces (Phase 2 baseline)

- `client.meaning.thesaurus` — CRUD + `sync_vocabulary` + `create_enterprise_override` + existing list/resolve/append
- `client.define.shapes` — `create` / `list` / `get` / `apply` / `align`
- `client.meaning.proposals` — `list` / `accept` / `reject` / `accept_batch` / `reject_batch`
- `client.meaning.bundles.import` (Python: `import_` — `import` is a keyword)

## Checklist when changing Node client APIs

1. Mirror methods on the Python sync + async classes (same `snake_case` names).
2. Wire facades in `python/src/loxtep/client.py` (`DefineFacade` / `MeaningFacade`).
3. Add or extend tests under `python/tests/`.
4. Bump `python/pyproject.toml` version + CHANGELOG when publishing a release.

```text
❌ Node PR merges shapes/proposals; Python still only has list_terms
✅ Same PR (or follow-up opened immediately) ports python/ + tests + docs
```
